  "description": "FAWLAS crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group A b a 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H112 Gd4 N8 O32 Zn8 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1A (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2A (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3A (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn4A (Zn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.120-3.991 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.70-112.55°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4Zn8(OH)8(L)8(O2CCHMe2)8](ClO4)4·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Gd(III), Zn(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
